  "interpretation_boundary": "The test uses the real default Doubler4 Stereo VST3 state found in the local host. Arrival clusters are peaks of a 0.35 ms moving-RMS envelope, separated by at least 2 ms; they describe energy concentrations rather than four perfectly isolated voice delays. The 80 Hz Range algorithm has an approximately 7 ms voice-path delay according to the official manual, while each voice also has its displayed delay. Host PDC, algorithmic effect timing, and displayed voice delay are therefore reported separately. Mono-fold delta is measured over each 0-65 ms impulse response relative to per-channel stereo RMS; it does not predict all musical material or modulation states."
